    "accuracy_baseline_model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash",
    "_baseline_note": "DeepSeek-V4.1 on the vLLM plugin. Three of these arguments are forced, not chosen: the runtime takes --kv-cache-dtype auto/bfloat16/nvfp4 and refuses the fp8 this harness supplies by default, prefix caching is refused because a block-table hit restores the compressed pages but not the per-request CSA2 state read alongside them (the harness already passes --no-enable-prefix-caching), and the two env vars are what keep cudagraph_mode at the FULL_AND_PIECEWISE the harness asks for instead of falling back to eager. max-model-len is 8192 because the checkpoint's own 1M would price the KV pool out of the box this was measured on. Baseline 0.9303 flexible-extract (strict identical) is one full 1319-question 20-shot run of this exact recipe, driven by .github/scripts/atom_oot_test.sh itself rather than a stand-in. One run, so read it as a point and not as a noise estimate: the 0.91 bar leaves 2pp, and a single red should be rerun before it is believed. This is the non-speculative cell; the DSpark one below shares every other argument, so the pair isolates speculation. Coverage boundary, since max-model-len reads like one and is not: 8192 is sized for the KV pool (the checkpoint's own max_position_embeddings is 1048576), not for what the indexer sees. Measured, the 20-shot prompts are 3411 tokens at p50 and 3736 at most, so the token-level selection is exercised -- index_topk is 512, picked out of ~3.4k, past a sliding_window of 128. The block-level candidate stage is not: candidate_topk_blocks (2048) x candidate_block_size (8) is 16384 tokens, which 8192 cannot reach, so that stage never discards anything here. Raising max-model-len would NOT close that -- gsm8k's prompts are 3.4k whatever the limit is. Covering it needs a long-context task, not a bigger flag."
